  "result": "`split_arg_string('cmd a#b')` now returns `['cmd', 'a#b']`. `python -m pytest tests/test_shell_completion.py -q` passes (59 tests).\n\n- **Fix:** in `src/click/shell_completion.py`, I set `lex.commenters = \"\"` on the shlex lexer inside `split_arg_string`. shlex treats `#` as a comment start by default, which is what dropped everything after it.\n- **Test:** I added `test_split_arg_string_hash_is_not_comment` to `tests/test_shell_completion.py`, plus an import for `split_arg_string`. It checks both `\"cmd a#b\"` and `\"cmd #b\"`, so a leading `#` is covered too.\n\nI didn't run the new test against the old code, so I haven't seen it fail without the fix. I haven't committed anything.",
